Repo: /Users/marcel.a.n.navarro/Dev/zimmermann-pwa. Branch: feature/SFCC-236_product-card-shared-component (already checked out). Steps 1-5 already committed (ZimmSlideIndicator, ZimmSizeChip+ZimmSizeChipGroup, ZimmProductPrice isLive, ZimmProductCardMedia, ZimmProductCardContent). Build Step 6 of the SFCC-236 plan — the final component, the organism that assembles everything.

## STANDING RULE FOR THIS ENTIRE TASK: no assumptions, everything traces to a real source
Every prior step in this build shipped defects that only surfaced when someone actually checked the real Figma node instead of trusting a plausible-sounding inference — wrong colours, wrong copy, wrong spacing, a completely missing responsive breakpoint, a misaligned row. All of those passed `tsc`/tests/lint and were only caught by a human or an agent actually pulling the Figma data and measuring the live DOM. For THIS step in particular — the one that assembles every other step's work — treat every visual/behavioural claim below as something to verify against the cited node, not as ground truth to copy blindly. If something you need is NOT cited below with a node ID, stop and report it as an open question rather than inventing a plausible value.

## Create ONLY these 3 files
```
overrides/app/components/ui-kits/organisms/zimmProductCard/index.tsx
overrides/app/components/ui-kits/organisms/zimmProductCard/index.stories.tsx
overrides/app/components/ui-kits/organisms/zimmProductCard/index.test.tsx
overrides/app/components/ui-kits/organisms/zimmProductCard/zimmProductCard.css.ts
```
(4 files, the standard set.) Plus register the recipe in `overrides/app/theme/components/index.ts` — one import, one entry. Do not touch any other file. Do NOT modify `zimmProductCardMedia/`, `zimmProductCardContent/`, `zimmSizeChip*/`, `zimmSlideIndicator/`, or `zimmProductPrice/` — compose them as-is, exactly as already committed.

## Read these FIRST, in full, before writing anything
1. `overrides/app/components/ui-kits/molecules/zimmProductCardMedia/index.tsx` + `.css.ts` — know its exact props, its `data-card-slot` values (`media`, `close`, `carousel`, `indicator`), and that it already handles the hover-capable-vs-touch split and keyboard operability internally. You compose it, you do not reimplement any of its behaviour.
2. `overrides/app/components/ui-kits/molecules/zimmProductCardContent/index.tsx` + `.css.ts` — know its exact props, its `data-card-slot` values (`content`, `price`, `sizeChips`), and that its `nameLink` renders a real `<a>` (via `chakra(RouteLink)`) wrapping only the product name — this is the ONLY anchor tag anywhere in the composed card, and it is your foundation for the stretched-link pattern below.
3. `overrides/app/components/ui-kits/molecules/zimmColourSwatchGroup/index.tsx` — general reference for how a molecule-composing organism structures itself in this codebase (though this build has no true organism-composing-two-molecules precedent yet — `zimmSubscribeSection` is the closest existing organism, skim it for the general shape: owns domain state, composes molecules, has its own recipe).

## Design source — confirmed via direct Figma inspection this session, cite these exact nodes
Figma file `wPiWmZZOVKnrENUWk2XWWm`. Component set `Product-card`, node `40000223:2822` (20 variants: Size × State × Type × Unavailable).

**The variation matrix — confirmed via `get_metadata`'s `hidden` attributes on the real assembled Card-content instances, not inferred:**

| Variation (`Type`) | Default state | Hover state |
|---|---|---|
| **Home** (`40000214:6141` default / `40002163:36593` hover) | image + name ONLY. Bag icon `hidden`. Attributes `hidden`. Price `hidden`. Size Selector `hidden`. | Price becomes visible (was hidden). Bag stays hidden. Size Selector stays hidden. Arrows appear (Media's own concern). |
| **PLP/PDP** (`40002163:41441` default / `40002163:41459` hover) | image + name + bag (always visible) + price. Attributes `hidden` (no colour/size on PLP). Size Selector `hidden`. | Price becomes `hidden`. Size Selector becomes visible (was hidden). Bag stays visible. Arrows appear. |
| **Wishlist** (`40002187:58446` default / `40002187:58458` hover) | image + name + bag (always visible) + Attributes visible (colour+size) + price. Size Selector `hidden`. | Price becomes `hidden`. Size Selector becomes visible (was hidden) — **confirmed via `get_metadata` on node `40002187:58460`: `Size Selector` has no `hidden` attribute at all in the Wishlist hover instance, identical to PLP's own hover reveal.** **This contradicts the literal Jira AC text for SFCC-236, which only mentions "image switches" and "arrows appear" for Wishlist hover and never mentions a size-selector reveal — the AC is incomplete, the design is the source of truth per AGENTS.md's doc-integrity rule, build to the design.** Arrows appear. |

**Unavailable=True**: confirmed only in scope for PLP/PDP per the AC text ("PLP variation... out of stock... notify me"; Recently-Viewed-Full-History explicitly "same behavior as PLP card"). Home and Wishlist ACs never mention an out-of-stock/notify-me treatment. Both `ZimmProductCardMedia` and `ZimmProductCardContent` already handle `isUnavailable` generically (bag disables) regardless of variation — nothing variation-specific needs to be added for Home/Wishlist's unavailable state; just pass `isUnavailable` through uniformly. Do not invent Home/Wishlist-specific unavailable behaviour beyond what Media/Content already do generically.

**"Recently Viewed Full History" is not a fourth variant** — the AC states it behaves identically to PLP, so it is `variation: 'plp'`. Do not add a fourth union member for it.

## Component contract — discriminated union, not a `variation` string switch anywhere in render logic

```ts
type ZimmProductCardImage = { src: string; alt: string }; // matches ZimmProductCardMediaImage — import that type, do not redeclare it

type ZimmProductCardBaseProps = {
  id: string;
  href: string; // PDP URL, pre-site-prefixed by the caller (page-level concern, not this organism's)
  name: string;
  headingLevel: /* whatever ZimmProductName's real `as` type is — import via ComponentProps, same pattern ZimmProductCardContent already established, do not redeclare */;
  primaryImage: ZimmProductCardImage;
  hoverImage?: ZimmProductCardImage;
  images?: ZimmProductCardImage[];
  currentPrice?: string;
  originalPrice?: string;
  isPriceLoading?: boolean;
  isUnavailable?: boolean;
  onNotifyMe?: () => void; // only meaningful when isUnavailable; Content already no-ops without a usable label internally, but this organism must supply SOME real, correct aria-label-worthy context — check exactly what ZimmProductCardContent needs
};

type ZimmProductCardPlpVariation = {
  variation: 'plp';
  onAddToBag?: () => void;
  sizeChipValues?: /* ZimmSizeChipValue[], import from zimmSizeChipGroup, do not redeclare */;
  selectedSizeChipValue?: string;
  onSizeChipSelect?: (value: string) => void;
};

type ZimmProductCardHomeVariation = {
  variation: 'home';
  // no additions — Home never shows bag, attributes, or size chips
};

type ZimmProductCardWishlistVariation = {
  variation: 'wishlist';
  colour: string; // required, not optional — wishlist AC always shows it
  size: string; // required
  onRemove: () => void; // required — a wishlist card with no way to remove itself is a spec violation
  onAddToBag?: () => void; // bag is always visible for wishlist per the confirmed matrix above
};

export type ZimmProductCardProps = ZimmProductCardBaseProps &
  (ZimmProductCardPlpVariation | ZimmProductCardHomeVariation | ZimmProductCardWishlistVariation);
```
Adjust exact shape only where composing the real child prop types demands it (e.g. if `ZimmProductCardMediaProps`'s `removeLabel` needs a specific string this organism must construct — check its real signature and wire it correctly, e.g. `removeLabel` should likely be built from `name`, something like "Remove {name} from wishlist" via `defineMessages` with an interpolated value, matching patterns already used in this build). Document any deviation from this sketch in your report.

## VARIATION_CONFIG — the mechanism that satisfies the extensibility AC

A module-level, plain object (NOT a function, not a class) mapping each `variation` value to the boolean/behavioural flags Media and Content need:
```ts
const VARIATION_CONFIG: Record<ZimmProductCardProps['variation'], {
  showBag: boolean;
  showAttributes: boolean;
  showSizeChips: boolean; // PLP and Wishlist both true, per the confirmed matrix
  hoverHidesPrice: boolean; // true for plp/wishlist, false for home
  hoverRevealsPrice: boolean; // true for home only
  hoverRevealsSizeSelector: boolean; // true for plp/wishlist, false for home
  showRemove: boolean; // wishlist only
}> = { /* ... */ };
```
**The render body must contain NO `switch`/`if` on `props.variation` anywhere.** Every layout/visibility decision reads from this object, keyed by `props.variation`. This is the actual, testable proof of the extensibility AC — adding a new variation later means adding a union member + one row to this object, touching no JSX. Your test file needs `@ts-expect-error` cases proving the union is enforced at compile time (e.g. `variation: 'wishlist'` without `onRemove`/`colour`/`size` must fail `tsc`; `variation: 'home'` given `onRemove` must fail `tsc`) — these are the extensibility AC's real proof, not just "the object exists."

## The stretched-link pattern — the trickiest part, get the layering right

The card holds MULTIPLE independently-clickable controls (bag, arrows, size chips, remove) plus one clickable name-link — nesting all of that inside a single big `<a>` is invalid HTML. The established pattern (already anticipated when `ZimmProductCardContent` built its own `nameLink` as the only real anchor in the whole composed tree):

1. **This organism's own root must be `position: relative`** and must establish the stacking context (`z-index: 0` or similar on the root, or simply rely on it being the nearest positioned ancestor — verify Chakra doesn't need an explicit z-index for this to work correctly).
2. **`ZimmProductCardContent`'s `nameLink` already renders the one real `<a>`.** This organism's OWN recipe (not Content's) must add a `::after` pseudo-element to that link via a descendant selector targeting Content's `nameLink` — e.g. something shaped like `[data-card-slot="content"] a::after { content: ''; position: absolute; inset: 0; }`. This `::after`'s `position: absolute` resolves against the nearest POSITIONED ancestor, which must be THIS ORGANISM'S ROOT (not Content's own root, not Media's own root) — for this to work, **verify** neither `ZimmProductCardContent`'s `root` part nor any of its internal wrapper divs sets `position: relative` (read the file to confirm — if you find one does, that's a real, reportable finding, not something to silently work around from here).
3. **Every genuinely-interactive control needs to sit ABOVE the stretched overlay**, or it becomes unclickable (the invisible `::after` overlay would intercept the click first). This means: the bag button, the remove button, the carousel arrows, and every size chip need `position: relative` + a z-index higher than the stretched link's `::after` (which has no explicit z-index, so it participates at the stacking order of its own element — verify what z-index value is actually needed here; the simplest correct approach is giving the interactive controls `zIndex: 1` and leaving the stretched link's `::after` at the default `auto`/0, but confirm this actually works by testing it, don't just assert it in a comment). **This is exactly the kind of thing that looks fine in a screenshot and is silently broken in reality** — a click test is the only real proof.
4. **Do NOT modify `ZimmProductCardMedia` or `ZimmProductCardContent` to add this CSS yourselves** — it must live entirely in THIS organism's own recipe, reaching in via `data-card-slot` descendant selectors, exactly matching the established "the organism's recipe root part selects descendants via data-card-slot, molecules stay agnostic" pattern already used for Media's own internal hover-reveal (`carousel`/`indicatorWrapper` gating lives in Media's OWN recipe, keyed off its OWN parts — but THIS cross-component reveal, name-link-stretches-to-cover-Media-too, has to live here, in the organism, since it spans both child components).

## Hover-reveal CSS — same technique as Step 4's Media, applied across BOTH composed children

Read Step 4's `zimmProductCardMedia.css.ts` for the established pattern: `@media (hover: hover) and (pointer: fine)` gates, `display`/visibility toggles keyed off `data-card-slot` values, and a structural test importing the REAL unmocked recipe object to prove the media-query behaviour (this build has now needed exactly this technique three times — Step 4's arrows/indicator, Step 4's Fix 1, and it will bite you here too if you skip it).

This organism's own recipe needs `[data-card-slot="content"] [data-card-slot="price"]` and `[data-card-slot="content"] [data-card-slot="sizeChips"]` reveal rules, gated by `(hover: hover) and (pointer: fine)` AND by which `variation` is active — but **the render body still must not switch on `variation` in JS**. Resolve this by having `VARIATION_CONFIG`'s `hoverHidesPrice`/`hoverRevealsPrice`/`hoverRevealsSizeSelector` flags become **props passed into `useMultiStyleConfig`** (the same technique `ZimmSizeChip`'s `disabled` prop and `ZimmProductCardContent`'s `disabled` prop already use to let the recipe branch on a boolean without the component's JSX branching) — the recipe's `baseStyle` function receives these flags and returns the correct conditional CSS, while `index.tsx`'s JSX itself stays uniform, always rendering both Media and Content with all their sub-parts, letting CSS decide what's visible.

**Below the desktop breakpoint (touch), none of this hover-reveal CSS should apply at all** — a touch device has no hover; Content's price/size-chip slots keep their default (non-hover) visibility state permanently on touch, matching how a mobile shopper would actually experience a card (no hover state exists to reveal anything). Verify this is the correct read by checking: does the AC or Figma actually specify a MOBILE-specific default for what's shown (e.g. does mobile PLP show price OR the size-selector by default, never both, since there's no hover to swap between them)? Check Figma's Mobile-size variants of the Product-card (`40002163:41477` PLP/PDP Mobile Default, or similar per the resolved variant table from earlier in this build) if you need to confirm this — do not assume, the same rule as everything else in this prompt.

## Recipe file (`zimmProductCard.css.ts`)
- `parts`: at minimum `['root']` plus whatever descendant-selector keys you need for the hover-reveal and stretched-link rules — since these are descendant selectors WITHIN `root`'s own style object (not separate Chakra "parts" in the useMultiStyleConfig sense), most of this recipe may only need `root` as its actual declared part, with everything else expressed as nested selectors inside `root`'s style object. Confirm this against how `recipeParts.test.ts` actually walks recipes — if it requires every `styles.X` read to have a matching declared part, and you only ever read `styles.root` in the JSX, then `parts: ['root']` alone is correct and sufficient; don't invent parts you don't actually read via `useMultiStyleConfig`'s returned object in `index.tsx`.
- Recipe key: `'ZimmProductCard'` — confirm it doesn't collide with any base SFCC recipe name (there is a base `ProductTile` recipe in `node_modules` — this is a different name, so you're safe, but double check per this build's own established caution here).
- All colour/spacing as `var(--zimm-*)`. No bare Chakra token keys. Responsive/pointer gating as explicit media queries only.

## Stories
`title: 'Commerce/ZimmProductCard'`. Mandatory `Default` export. Named exports covering AT MINIMUM: `PLP`, `PLPOutOfStock`, `Home`, `Wishlist`, `SingleImage`, `MultipleImages`. Each hover-dependent story needs a doc comment telling a human reviewer exactly what to check by hovering (since Storybook's own test runner can't force a `(hover: hover)` media context — same limitation Step 4 already documented). No `play` function asserting hover for the same reason Step 4 skipped it.

## Tests
Vitest + RTL. Cover:
- The two `@ts-expect-error` compile-time union cases (this is the extensibility AC's real proof).
- AC1 equivalent: primary image renders for all three variations × unavailable true/false (six cases) — assert via whatever Media renders through.
- **Exactly one `<a>` per card** — `getAllByRole('link')` returns length 1, regardless of variation.
- Every interactive control (bag, arrows if multi-image, size chips if PLP/wishlist, remove if wishlist) remains SEPARATELY focusable and clickable — don't just check they're in the DOM, actually fire a click/keydown on each and confirm the right callback fires, proving the stretched-link z-index layering doesn't swallow their clicks. **This is the single most important test in this whole step** — if this passes falsely (e.g. because jsdom doesn't enforce real stacking-context click interception the way a browser does), say so explicitly in your report as a known limitation requiring a real-browser check, do not claim more confidence than jsdom can actually provide.
- The real-recipe structural test technique (unmocked import) proving the hover-reveal media query exists and is keyed correctly, same as Step 4's Fix 1 and Step 5's padding fix.
- No `switch`/`if` on `props.variation` anywhere in `index.tsx` — you can't easily assert this via a runtime test; instead make this trivially auditable by a human (keep the file's control flow simple enough that grepping for `variation ===` or `switch (variation)` returns zero hits in the render body, and say so in your report).

## House rules
TypeScript only. Australian spelling. No `any` without a comment. No non-null assertion without a comment. No hardcoded design-value literal outside `var(--zimm-*)`. No `console.log`. Do not modify `package.json`.

## When done — report precisely
1. Exact file list with line counts.
2. Confirm nothing outside the 4 files + registration was touched.
3. The EXACT stretched-link CSS you wrote, and what you actually tested to confirm the z-index layering works (not just "it should work").
4. Whether the Mobile-default-state check (for the "no hover-reveal CSS on touch" question) turned up anything Figma-specific, and what you found.
5. All these clean:
```
npx tsc --noEmit
npx vitest run overrides/app/components/ui-kits/organisms/zimmProductCard
npx vitest run overrides/app/components/ui-kits/recipeParts.test.ts
npx vitest run overrides/app/theme/components/recipeGuards.test.ts
npx eslint overrides/app/components/ui-kits/organisms/zimmProductCard overrides/app/theme/components/index.ts
node scripts/auditTokenUsage.mjs
npm run test
```
Baseline going into this step: 51 files / 793 tests. Report the new total. Do NOT stage or commit anything — this step gets a real-browser visual and interaction check before it's considered done.

